00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:10.440 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  I'm sorry chicken and I'm the chairman  of the Shotley heritage peer project the  short leap here is over and I'm 22 years  old most local people would love to be  able to walk on it go fishing crabbing  and board boats what it was built for in  the first place  volunteers not see crucial we have no  paid staff at all at the moment and we  hope to employ people in the future it  was vital from the very beginning the  Baber and this account for got involved  and we were very fortunate because they  paid for a survey and decided with us  what was the best way forward I broached  with my colleagues the possibility of  the council buying the pier but we  reckoned it would not fit in with our  strategy basically we can't just keep  putting money where we'd like to and  when a group encouraged by Derrick Davis  was set up locally to buy and restore  here we were very much supportive of  that it's obviously a project which is  going to benefit the community when it's  when it's completed it will be somewhere  where people can enjoy themselves for us  also it will help to raise the tone of  the whole foreshore and that is in the  interest of well that as a  administration it's also in the interest  of the local community our group is  certainly an exemplar at every stage  we've talked the Baber and kept them  involved with what we're aiming to do  and I think that's the lesson I would  pass to other groups is talk food the  district councillors talk to the  officers because they are listening and  they do want what's best of a bur and  our area and to have that support and  the kind of expertise on how to fly to  grow and how to bid for things that has  helped us secure the first hundred  thousand pounds that we need we did get  an economic development grants of 20,000  pounds from Baber to help us develop the  plans I would like to say thank you too  baby you're doing a fine job liaison  with us and keep up the good work  we're in the grounds of Bentley's first  cooperative pub have raised a hundred  thousand pounds and we have built a shop  which is now run by 45 volunteers from  all aspects of the village the store is  volunteers all the people serving all  the people buying everybody as a  volunteer it was needed because eleven  years ago our village stall closed and  we've had nothing since paper District  Council have been exceedingly helpful  their community team helped us through  the process of getting a capital grant  from Weber they also identified the  princes countryside fund which was the  catalyst money that arrived and we were  able to start work in February and open  in July so we have been greatly helped  by the community team at Weber without  it I would probably be still standing in  a car park waiting for the rest of the  funding I would like to express my  thanks to the Babel communities team for  all their help and advice which has  proved vital in our bid to open a  community shop we had a really tall in  West thought which had served its  purpose was been here since 1978 and it  was in fairly sorry state and that was  really what made us start to think can  we raise the money to build a new  village hall without the volunteers we  wouldn't be here the village hall  committee has done a tremendous amount  all voluntary the project manager and  architect has given all these time for  free but then so have lots of other  people out of the village you know we've  had a lot of help from other  organisations lots of advice lots of  support the counts have been fantastic  from very early on we made a  relationship with them they've advised  us all the way through lots of different  departments have come out and talk to us  or spoken to us on the phone we've met  with them  and we've also had a substantial grant  from mid Suffolk District Council the  offices have been various available to  us all the way through they've been very  very good in all aspects that we've  needed to deal with and they advised us  on applying for grants to other  organisations but we had a big grant  from the mid Suffolk District Council  which totaled twenty five thousand  pounds  that was apart from the help we've had  from our district counselor and the  county counselor it was it was an honor  but also it was fairly easy you've got  one side one hand which has got very lot  of talented people who have moved into  Westhoff village where the architect  there's a landscaper and that's where it  started on the other hand upstairs here  you've got a dedicated and a very  efficient community team and the  planning officers as well who has has  gopher planning so they have to be  involved as well so you've got those two  things it's really like two hands we put  them together you pray for a start and  then you see you open them up and you  see what comes down it's been rebuilt by  the village by the community they were  very very good at using their local  talents it is absolutely wonderful as an  example to us all and many many villages  that are now looking towards doing the  same we'd like to say a very big thank  you for everything you've done for us  and the support in all kinds of areas  that you've given us throughout this  project and of course for the financial  help which has made a big difference  thank you very much  you  you  [Music]

